  "note": "Municipal elections, 17 May 1961; Central Ward was the only contest. West Ward was settled at the withdrawals (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1961, p. 10). East Ward (seven seats) was uncontested, but its members are not printed in the sources searched, so it is not recorded. The paper prints 'seven Unionists were elected' and gives each name surname-first; the candidates are listed here in the paper's order with the printed form preserved. N. Sweeney is printed as Independent and ex-Service."
